# Title chips

Stack chips (`.sbadge`) use the OKLCH tokens already in `:root`. Do not set `--pill-c` to a hex color.

- One word inside each chip. Put the rest of the label in the sentence under the row.
- The chip border uses `var(--line)`. Define `--line` on the page.
- The row wraps (`flex-wrap: wrap`). Do not set `white-space: nowrap` on `.sbadge`.
- At `760px`, `body` uses `background-attachment: scroll`.
- Leave the hex colors in the lesson paragraphs. They are examples, not chips.
- Each finished page's chip colors live in `DONE` in `scripts/check-chips.py`. To restyle a guide, change that one guide and move its line from `LEGACY` to `DONE`.
- Do not add a new script, workflow, or rule per page. One guide per pull request.
- A new guide must not copy hex chips from the skeleton.
